he mean squared error of the model:\n\n$$\n\\text{MSE}=\\frac{1}{n-2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({y}_{i}-{\\overset{^}{\\,y}}_{i})^{2}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\overset{^}{\\,y}}_{i}$ is the estimate of ${y}_{i}$ given by our regression model.\n\n- ${S}_{xx}$ is the usual sum of squares formula:\n\n$$\n{S}_{xx}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2}\n$$\n\nTo construct the confidence interval, we proceed as follows:\n\n- **Step 1.** Find the point estimate. From the regression equation $\\overset{^}{\\,y}=3.4+1.8x,$ our point estimate is\n\n$$\n{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}=1.8.\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the margin of error. Since we are interested in finding a $90%$ confidence interval, we have \n\n$$\n\\alpha =1-0.9=0.1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\alpha }{2}=0.05.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $P(T>1.812)=0.05.$ As a result, \n\n$$\n{t}_{n-2,\\alpha /2}={t}_{10,0.05}=1.812.\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the margin of error:\n\n$$\n{t}_{n-2,\\alpha /2}\\cdot \\text{SE}[{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}\\,]=1.812\\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{11.5}{143}}≈0.5\n$$\n\n- **Step 3.** Determine the limits of the confidence interval:\n\n$$\n{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}\\,\\pm \\,{t}_{n-2,\\alpha /2}\\cdot \\text{SE}[{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}\\,]=1.8\\pm 0.5\n$$"] ["question-42368253-8090-5197-973b-1010d704c08f" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-5dbbd93d-093b-57e4-bfc1-ad59a17bdad5" :answer-field/id #uuid "5dbbd93d-093b-57e4-bfc1-ad59a17bdad5"] ["answer-923c151e-4c0c-5138-872f-79d725e9b5a7" :answer/id #uuid "923c151e-4c0c-5138-872f-79d725e9b5a7"] ["answer-923c151e-4c0c-5138-872f-79d725e9b5a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-923c151e-4c0c-5138-872f-79d725e9b5a7" :answer/value "1.3\\pm 0.1"] ["answer-9e7cbdf0-9605-52c2-aebb-1c3a606aa1d2" :answer/id #uuid "9e7cbdf0-9605-52c2-aebb-1c3a606aa1d2"] ["answer-9e7cbdf0-9605-52c2-aebb-1c3a606aa1d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9e7cbdf0-9605-52c2-aebb-1c3a606aa1d2" :answer/value "1.5\\pm 0.4"] ["answer-8182d4e1-5154-5473