-9a0fa4ee-d860-5a97-91a9-24370dbc9085" :question/math-academy-id "q-159376"] ["question-9a0fa4ee-d860-5a97-91a9-24370dbc9085" :question/problem "Let $\\overset{^}{\\,y}={\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{0}+{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}x=2.4+0.2x$ be the regression line fitted using a sample $({x}_{1},{y}_{1}),\\,…,\\,({x}_{12},{y}_{12})$ of $n=12$ paired observations. Assuming that all conditions for the simple regression model are satisfied, the mean square error of the model is $0.7,$ and ${S}_{xx}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2}=18.9,$ find a $95%$ confidence interval for the slope of the regression line.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(T>2.228)=0.025,$ where $T$ has a student's $t$-distribution with $10$ degrees of freedom. Also, the standard error for ${\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}\\,]=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\text{MSE}}{{S}_{xx}}}.\n$$\n\n*"] ["question-9a0fa4ee-d860-5a97-91a9-24370dbc9085" :question/worked-solution "We use the following notations:\n\n- $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x$ is the regression line that best fits the population, and\n\n- $\\overset{^}{\\,y}={\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{0}+{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}x$ is the estimate of the \"true\" regression line given by the data in our sample.\n\nIn this case, we have that  \n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{\\,y}={\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{0}+{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}x=2.4+0.2x.\n$$\n\nWe are told that all assumptions for a simple regression model are held. So, given a value $\\alpha $ between $0$ and $1,$ the corresponding $[100(1-\\alpha )]%$ confidence interval for the slope ${\\beta }_{1}$ of our model can be written as\n\n$$\n{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}\\,\\pm \\,\\overset{\\text{margin of error}}{\\overset{⏞}{{t}_{n-2,\\alpha /2}\\cdot \\text{SE}[{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}\\,]}}.\n$$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- $\\,{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}$ is our point estimate for the slope, computed using the data points from our sample.\n\n- $P(T>{t}_{n-2,\\alpha /2})=\\frac{\\alpha }{2},$ where $T$ has a student's $t$-distribution with $n-2$ degrees of freedom.\n\n- $\\text{SE}[{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}\\,]$ is the standard error of ${\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1},$ given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}\\,]=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\text{MSE}}{{S}_{xx}}}\n$$\n\nwhere we have:\n\n- $\\text{MSE}$ is the mean squared error of the model:\n\n$$\n\\text{MSE}=\\frac{1}{n-2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({y}_{i}-{\\overset{^}{\\,y}}_{i})^{2}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\overset{^}{\\,y}}_{i}$ is the estimate of ${y}_{i}$ given by our regression model.\n\n- ${S}_{xx}$ is the usual sum of squares formula:\n\n$$\n{S}_{xx}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2}\n$$\n\nTo construct the confidence interval, we proceed as follows:\n\n- **Step 1.** Find the point estimate. From the regression equation $\\overset{^}{\\,y}=2.4+0.2x,$ our point estimate is\n\n$$\n{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}=0.2.\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the margin of error. Since we are interested in finding a $95%$ confidence interval, we have \n\n$$\n\\alpha =1-0.95=0.05\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\alpha }{2}=0.025.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $P(T>2.228)=0.025.$ As a result, \n\n$$\n{t}_{n-2,\\alpha /2}={t}_{10,0.025}=2.228.\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the margin of error:\n\n$$\n{t}_{n-2,\\alpha /2}\\cdot \\text{SE}[{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}\\,]=2.228\\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{0.7}{18.9}}≈0.4\n$$\n\n- **Step 3.** Determine the limits of the confidence interval:\n\n$$\n{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}\\,\\pm \\,{t}_{n-2,\\alpha /2}\\cdot \\text{SE}[{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}\\,]=0.2\\pm 0.4\n$$"] ["question-9a0fa4ee-d860-5a97-91a9-24370dbc9085" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-3cfd90c1-e81f-5461-89ae-4d8978dbf8e2" :answer-field/id #uuid "3cfd90c1-e81f-5461-89ae-4d8978dbf8e2"] ["answer-278a0133-b0b4-5d1a-81b8-49903ddff8ed" :answer/id #uuid "278a0133-b0b4-5d1a-81b8-49903ddff8ed"] ["answer-278a0133-b0b4-5d1a-81b8-49903ddff8ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-278a0133-b0b4-5d1a-81b8-49903ddff8ed" :answer/value "0.2\\pm 0.1"] ["answer-80cf0bd5-fc8a-5eed-99c9-1117dae18dbf" :answer/id #uuid "80cf0bd5-fc8a-5eed-99c9-1117dae18dbf"] ["answer-80cf0bd5-fc8a-5eed-99c9-1117dae18dbf" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-80cf0bd5-fc8a-5eed-99c9-1117dae18dbf" :answer/value "0.2\\pm 0.2"] ["answer-508865b1-77ef-551a-a36f-b6776f0a785e" :answer/id #uuid "508865b1-77ef-551a-a36f-b6776f0a785e"] ["answer-508865b1-77ef-551a-a36f-b6776f0a785e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-508865b1-77ef-551a-a36f-b6776f0a785e" :answer/value "0.2\\pm 0.3"] ["answer-c4b5686d-bff3-5555-ae5d-0690a2f7e5ee" :answer/id #uuid "c4b5686d-bff3-5555-ae5d-0690a2f7e5ee"] ["answer-c4b5686d-bff3-5555-ae5d-0690a2f7e5ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c4b5686d-bff3-5555-ae5d-0690a2f7e5ee" :answer/value "0.2\\pm 0.4"] ["answer-5db73e1c-4ac3-5171-b6a5-b6b7072792bc" :answer/id #uuid "5db73e1c-4ac3-5171-b6a5-b6b7072792bc"] ["answer-5db73e1c-4ac3-5171-b6a5-b6b7072792bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5db73e1c-4ac3-5171-b6a5-b6b7072792bc" :answer/value "0.2\\pm 0.6"] ["answer-field-3cfd90c1-e81f-5461-89ae-4d8978dbf8e2" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-3cfd90c1-e81f-5461-89ae-4d8978dbf8e2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-3cfd90c1-e81f-5461-89ae-4d8978dbf8e2" :answer-field/correct "answer-c4b5686d-bff3-5555-ae5d-0690a2f7e5ee"] ["answer-field-3cfd90c1-e81f-5461-89ae-4d8978dbf8e2" :answer-field/choices "answer-278a0133-b0b4-5d1a-81b8-49903ddff8ed"] ["answer-field-3cfd90c1-e81f-5461-89ae-4d8978dbf8e2" :answer-field/choices "answer-80cf0bd5-fc8a-5eed-99c9-1117dae18dbf"] ["answer-field-3cfd90c1-e81f-5461-89ae-4d8978dbf8e2" :answer-field/choices "answer-508865b1-77ef-551a-a36f-b6776f0a785e"] ["answer-field-3cfd90c1-e81f-5461-89ae-4d8978dbf8e2" :answer-field/choices "answer-c4b5686d-bff3-5555-ae5d-0690a2f7e5ee"] ["answer-field-3cfd90c1-e81f-5461-89ae-4d8978dbf8e2" :answer-f