nce interval for the slope ${\\beta }_{1}$ of our model can be written as\n\n$$\n{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}\\,\\pm \\,\\overset{\\text{margin of error}}{\\overset{⏞}{{t}_{n-2,\\alpha /2}\\cdot \\text{SE}[{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}\\,]}}.\n$$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- $\\,{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}$ is our point estimate for the slope, computed using the data points from our sample.\n\n- $P(T>{t}_{n-2,\\alpha /2})=\\frac{\\alpha }{2},$ where $T$ has a student's $t$-distribution with $n-2$ degrees of freedom.\n\n- $\\text{SE}[{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}\\,]$ is the standard error of ${\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1},$ given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}\\,]=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\text{MSE}}{{S}_{xx}}}\n$$\n\nwhere we have:\n\n- $\\text{MSE}$ is the mean squared error of the model:\n\n$$\n\\text{MSE}=\\frac{1}{n-2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({y}_{i}-{\\overset{^}{\\,y}}_{i})^{2}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\overset{^}{\\,y}}_{i}$ is the estimate of ${y}_{i}$ given by our regression model.\n\n- ${S}_{xx}$ is the usual sum of squares formula:\n\n$$\n{S}_{xx}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2}\n$$\n\nTo construct the confidence interval, we proceed as follows:\n\n- **Step 1.** Find the point estimate. From the regression equation $\\overset{^}{\\,y}=3.4-0.6x,$ our point estimate is\n\n$$\n{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}=-0.6.\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the margin of error. Since we are interested in finding a $90%$ confidence interval, we have \n\n$$\n\\alpha =1-0.9=0.1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\alpha }{2}=0.05.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $P(T>1.895)=0.05.$ As a result, \n\n$$\n{t}_{n-2,\\alpha /2}={t}_{7,0.05}=1.895.\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the margin of error:\n\n$$\n{t}_{n-2,\\alpha /2}\\cdot \\text{SE}[{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}\\,]=1.895\\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{1.16}{240}}≈0.1\n$$\n\n- **Step 3.** Determine the limits of the confidence interval:\n\n$$\n{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}\\,\\pm \\,{t}_{n-2,\\alpha /2}\\cdot \\text{SE}[{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}\\,]=-0.6\\pm 0.1\n$$"] ["question-f28f1c0e-4ffd-5dee-98b7-1c475d5129ec" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-04602db9-708b-5fcf-bfdb-6de19a2849cc" :answer-field/id #uuid "04602db9-708b-5fcf-bfdb-6de19a2849cc"] ["answer-00f51304-e3b6-5932-ad51-bd19b9045d67" :answer/id #uuid "00f51304-e3b6-5932-ad51-bd19b9045d67"] ["answer-00f51304-e3b6-5932-ad51-bd19b9045d67" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-00f51304-e3b6-5932-ad51-bd19b9045d67" :answer/value "-0.6\\pm 0.1"] ["answer-0a29929b-8aeb-5e21-9031-f1ccdab60a1c" :answer/id #uuid "0a29929b-8aeb-5e21-9031-f1ccdab60a1c"] ["answer-0a29929b-8aeb-5e21-9031-f1ccdab60a1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0a29929b-8aeb-5e21-9031-f1ccdab60a1c" :answer/value "-0.6\\pm 0.3"] ["answer-db665bb1-2442-5540-9fe3-cca6ff6884bc" :answer/id #uuid "db665bb1-2442-5540-9fe3-cca6ff6884bc"] ["answer-db665bb1-2442-5540-9fe3-cca6ff6884bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-db665bb1-2442-5540-9fe3-cca6ff6884bc" :answer/value "-0.6\\pm 0.5"] ["answer-d7bc35a1-e944-560a-a330-d31779067a9c" :answer/id #uuid "d7bc35a1-e944-560a-a330-d31779067a9c"] ["answer-d7bc35a1-e944-560a-a330-d31779067a9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d7bc35a1-e944-560a-a330-d31779067a9c" :answer/value "-0.6\\pm 0.8"] ["answer-49fa42a9-46e5-5910-9c55-1b9972e31902" :answer/id #uuid "49fa42a9-46e5-5910-9c55-1b9972e31902"] ["answer-49fa42a9-46e5-5910-9c55-1b9972e31902" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-49fa42a9-46e5-5910-9c55-1b9972e31902" :answer/value "-0.6\\pm 1.1"] ["answer-field-04602db9-708b-5fcf-bfdb-6de19a2849cc" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-04602db9-708b-5fcf-bfdb-6de19a2849cc" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-04602db9-708b-5fcf-bfdb-6de19a2849cc" :answer-field/correct "answer-00f51304-e3b6-5932-ad51-bd19b9045d67"] ["answer-field-04602db9-708b-5fcf-bfdb-6de19a2849cc" :answer-field/choices "answer-00f51304-e3b6-5932-ad51-bd19b9045d67"] ["answer-field-04602db9-708b-5fcf-